<h1>Build a call queue with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">The afterlife has a waiting room, and its phone line works the same way. Callers take a number and hold, hearing announcements while they wait; caseworkers call the same number to take whoever has waited longest. It runs on three documents published on voiceml.org, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/verbs/enqueue/">&lt;Enqueue&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "list-check" %}</span>
			<h3>A place in line</h3>
			<p><code>&lt;Enqueue&gt;</code> puts each caller in a named queue, first come, first served.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "clock" %}</span>
			<h3>Announcements on hold</h3>
			<p>A hold document plays a message, pauses, and repeats until a caseworker is free.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "headset" %}</span>
			<h3>Agents take the next caller</h3>
			<p>A caseworker who calls in is connected to whoever has waited longest, with <code>&lt;Dial&gt;&lt;Queue&gt;</code>.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "telephone" %}</span>
			<h3>A word before connecting</h3>
			<p>The caller hears &ldquo;your number has been called&rdquo; just before the two are connected.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the pieces fit</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>Components of the waiting room line</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Piece</th>
					<th scope="col">Where it lives</th>
					<th scope="col">What it does</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Main document</td><td>voiceml.org, <code>/r/</code> URL</td><td>The number&rsquo;s voice URL. Puts callers in the queue and connects caseworkers to them.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Hold document</td><td>voiceml.org, <code>/s/</code> URL</td><td>The <code>waitUrl</code> of the <code>&lt;Enqueue&gt;</code>. Plays while a caller waits, over and over.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Connect document</td><td>voiceml.org, <code>/s/</code> URL</td><td>The <code>url</code> of the <code>&lt;Queue&gt;</code>. Plays to the caller just before they are connected.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Caseworkers&rsquo; phones</td><td>Any phone numbers</td><td>Call the same number to take the next caller.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Before you start</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>A VoiceML account with a phone number.</strong> See <a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> or <a href="/signup/">start a free trial</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>The numbers your agents call from</strong>, in E.164 format.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
		<p><strong>The caseworker numbers in this document are fictional.</strong> They use the 555-0100 to 555-0199 range, which is set aside for fiction. Replace them with your agents&rsquo; numbers before you publish.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the hold and connect documents</h2>
	<p>Publish both at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a>. Neither contains Liquid, so each is served from an <code>/s/</code> URL. Keep the URLs exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included, and don&rsquo;t post them publicly.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">wait.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["afterlife-queue"].wait | escape }}</code></pre>
	<p class="code-block-header">connect.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["afterlife-queue"].connect | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Publish the main document and point the number at it</h2>
	<p>Replace <code>WAIT_URL</code> and <code>CONNECT_URL</code> with the URLs from step 1, and the caseworker numbers with your agents&rsquo;. Publish it, and set the <code>/r/</code> URL it returns as the phone number&rsquo;s voice URL.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">main.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["afterlife-queue"].main | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 3: Test it</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Call from a phone that isn&rsquo;t on the caseworker list. You are asked to take a number and hear the hold announcements.</li>
		<li>From a caseworker phone, call the same number. The waiting caller hears &ldquo;Your number has been called,&rdquo; and the two of you are connected.</li>
		<li>Call from a caseworker phone again with nobody waiting. After ten seconds, you hear the goodbye.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the queue works</h2>
	<p>Both sides use the same queue name, <code>recently-deceased</code>. Queues are private to your account, so another account using the same name gets a separate queue.</p>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>The two halves of the queue</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Side</th>
					<th scope="col">Markup</th>
					<th scope="col">What happens</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Caller</td><td><code>&lt;Enqueue waitUrl="&hellip;"&gt;</code></td><td>The caller joins the back of the queue. The hold document is fetched and played, then fetched and played again, until a caseworker takes the call or the caller hangs up.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Caseworker</td><td><code>&lt;Dial timeout="10"&gt;&lt;Queue url="&hellip;"&gt;</code></td><td>The caller who has waited longest leaves the queue, hears the connect document, and is connected to the caseworker. With nobody waiting, the dial gives up after ten seconds.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>Caseworkers are recognized by <code>From</code>, using the same Liquid list check as the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-call-screening-with-voiceml/">call screening example</a>. Neither side has an <code>action</code>, so when a call ends, each document carries on to its goodbye.</p>
	<p>To play music instead of announcements, leave <code>waitUrl</code> out: callers then hear the platform&rsquo;s default hold playlist.</p>
</section>

