<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>No position announcements.</strong> The hold document is fetched with the caller&rsquo;s place in line and the queue&rsquo;s wait times, but a voiceml.org document can&rsquo;t read those values. Announcing &ldquo;you are caller number 3&rdquo; needs a hold document served from your own server.</li>
		<li><strong>Callers leave by hanging up.</strong> This hold document doesn&rsquo;t offer a way to leave the line or leave a message instead.</li>
		<li><strong>Agents pull calls; calls aren&rsquo;t pushed to them.</strong> A caller waits until a caseworker phones in. To ring agents as soon as someone joins, use the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-an-on-call-escalation-line-with-voiceml/">on-call escalation example</a> instead.</li>
		<li><strong>Waiting callers don&rsquo;t survive a platform restart.</strong> Queues are kept in memory, so a restart drops the callers waiting in them.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

